    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nThe Anthropic Messages API (`/v1/messages`) supports a `\"document\"` content\r\nblock type (introduced mid-2024) for native PDF / plain-text document ingestion.\r\nSGLang's Anthropic-compatible endpoint previously raised a validation error or\r\nsilently dropped such blocks, breaking clients that send document content\r\n(e.g., Claude SDK users passing PDF files).\r\n\r\nThis PR adds first-class support for the `document` block type so that\r\nSGLang no longer rejects these requests.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n**`python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/anthropic/protocol.py`**\r\n- Added `DocumentBlockSource` model supporting `base64`, `text`, and `url`\r\n  source types (matching the Anthropic API schema).\r\n- Added `DocumentBlock` model with optional `title`, `context`, `citations`\r\n  and `source` fields.\r\n- Registered `DocumentBlock` in the `AnthropicContentBlock` discriminated\r\n  union so Pydantic can parse it correctly.\r\n\r\n**`python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/anthropic/serving.py`**\r\n- Added handling for `block.type == \"document\"` in the message conversion\r\n  pipeline with a best-effort text fallback strategy:\r\n  - `text` source → content is passed through directly as a `text` part.\r\n  - `base64` source → emits a notice that binary content cannot be decoded by\r\n    local models.\r\n  - `url` source → emits the URL so the model has context about the document.\r\n  - `title` / `context` fields are prepended when present.\r\n\r\n> **Note:** Local models cannot natively parse binary PDFs, so this\r\n> implementation intentionally falls back to text representation rather than\r\n> attempting PDF decoding.\r\n\r\n## Contributors\r\n\r\nEngine Architecture Group 5, Engine Infrastructure Department, Xiaohongshu (RedNote):\r\nZhang Biao, Luo Zhaokai, Zhang Bing, Chenchen Hong.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nNo model-output changes for standard text / image requests — the new code\r\npath is only triggered when `\"type\": \"document\"` blocks are present.\r\n\r\nManual verification:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# text source — content passed through\r\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:30000/v1/messages \\\r\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r\n  -d '{\r\n    \"model\": \"...\",\r\n    \"max_tokens\": 64,\r\n    \"messages\": [{\r\n      \"role\": \"user\",\r\n      \"content\": [{\r\n        \"type\": \"document\",\r\n        \"source\": {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello from a document.\"},\r\n        \"title\": \"Test Doc\"\r\n      }]\r\n    }]\r\n  }'\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #29327989850](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29327989850)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #29327989564](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/29327989564)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
